  "prefLabel": "Plc 102.19 License",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 102.19 “License” means “license” as defined in RSA 310:2, I(f), reprinted in Appendix B. The term includes initial, renewal, conditional, and temporary licenses issued to practitioners or apprentices, and any similar form of approval required to practice a regulated profession in any jurisdiction.\n\nSource. #14135, eff 12-1-24 (formerly Plc 202.19)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc100-200.html"
